  "methodology": "Other",
  "methodology_other": "Data were collected from the Syria Population and Housing Census 2004, the 2004 Census Population Bulletin - Man and Nah from the Central Bureau of Statistics, the 2004 Census Tables of Building Characteristics by Area, the 2011 Statistical Abstract of Syria, the 2015 Statistical Abstract of Syria, the 2017 Statistical Abstract of Syria, Forced Dispersion: A Demographic Report on Human Status in Syria, the Syrian Arab Republic: IDP Movements Table, the Syrian Arab Republic Governorates Profile, and the Syrian Arab Republic 2018 Humanitarian Needs Overview. Census Bureau staff altered boundaries and modified the statistical data as detailed in the Metadata tab of the tabular data.",
  "name": "syria-subnational-boundaries-and-tabular-data",
  "notes": "The geodatabase contains boundaries for the national and first-, second-, and third-order administrative divisions, aligned to the Large Scale International Boundaries dataset from the U.S. Department of State. The feature classes are suitable for linking to the attribute data provided.\r\n\r\nThe tabular data contain total population for 2004 (census) and 2011, 2014, and 2016 (population estimates), as well as five-year age group and sex, and information relating to ethnicity, housing, access to services, forced dispersion, IDP movements, and people in need. ",
